  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukrenergo Transmission Network Emergency Restoration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The provision of up to EUR 300 million sovereign-guaranteed loan to the  National Energy Company Ukrenergo (&quot;Ukrenergo&quot; or the &quot;Company&quot;) aimed at  restoring the Ukrainian power transmission grid that was severely damaged by  Russian bombings. The loan consists of up to EUR 150 million for procurement of  equipment to implement emergency repairs of Ukrainian power transmission system  and up to EUR 150 million of capital structure support (the &quot;Project&quot;). The  EBRD loan is supported by the donor &quot;funded guarantee&quot; of up to 50% provided by  the United States through its contribution to the EBRD Crisis Response Special  Fund (the &quot;Crisis Fund&quot;). Furthermore, the loan is also complemented by an  investment grant of EUR 70.6 million provided by the Netherlands via the Crisis  Fund.  In addition to the financing package of EUR 370.6 million mentioned above,  the Project will be complemented by an additional capital structure support  loan of up to EUR 150 million to the Company together with donor-funded credit  enhancement.  The Project will strengthen the Company&apos;s financial position, enable Ukrenergo  to secure uninterrupted energy supply to the population and businesses  throughout the country and ensure the stability of the country&apos;s energy system,  which is strategically important particularly at the time of war. The Project  will also strengthen the Ukrainian power system&apos;s ability to maintain  commercial flows with ENTSO-E. The support package provided to the Company is  also important for safeguarding Ukrenergo&apos;s human capital, sustaining the  livelihoods of its vast workforce and delivering support for those most  affected under the ongoing wartime conditions. The Project will also enhance  power market reforms, required to improve financial stability of the energy  sector.</narrative>
  </description>
